{# The note a chief gives a stay — five stars, clicked.

   It used to be a select. A rating out of five is read as stars
   everywhere it is SHOWN on this module (_stars.html.twig, the place
   sheet, every camp card); asking for it through a dropdown made the one
   screen where the number is given the only one that spoke another
   language, and cost two taps on a phone for what is one.

   Five radios of the same group, no JavaScript: the stars ARE the
   control. A label is what the browser activates its radio from, so a tap
   anywhere on a star selects it; arrow keys move through the group in
   reading order because the radios are in that order in the DOM; and the
   accessible name of each one says the number out loud, which five
   identical shapes never could.

   « Pas de note » is a sixth radio in the same group rather than a reset
   button, and it is not decoration: a comment without a number is a
   normal, complete review (a chief who has nothing to quantify must not
   have to invent a number), and it is the only way back once a star has
   been clicked.

   Params:
     field_id    id prefix — each radio gets `{field_id}-{1..5}`, and the
                 « pas de note » one `{field_id}-none`
     field_name  posted name, the same on all six
     value       the rating currently stored, or null
     label       the legend
     help        optional, wired to the group with aria-describedby
     max         the top of the scale, Review::MAX_RATING
#}
{% set _help_id = field_id ~ '-help' %}
<fieldset class="{{ wrapper_class is defined ? wrapper_class : 'mb-3' }}"
          {%- if help|default('') %} aria-describedby="{{ _help_id }}"{% endif %}>
    <legend class="form-label small">{{ label }}</legend>
    <div class="d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center gap-2">
        <div class="rating-input">
            {% for i in 1..max %}
                <span class="rating-input-star">
                    <input type="radio" name="{{ field_name }}" id="{{ field_id }}-{{ i }}"
                           value="{{ i }}" autocomplete="off"{{ value == i ? ' checked' : '' }}>
                    <label for="{{ field_id }}-{{ i }}" title="{{ i }} / {{ max }}">
                        <i class="bi bi-star" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <i class="bi bi-star-fill" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <span class="visually-hidden">{{ i }} étoile{{ i > 1 ? 's' : '' }} sur {{ max }}</span>
                    </label>
                </span>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <input type="radio" class="btn-check" name="{{ field_name }}" id="{{ field_id }}-none"
               value="" autocomplete="off"{{ value is null ? ' checked' : '' }}>
        <label class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" for="{{ field_id }}-none">Pas de note</label>
    </div>
    {% if help|default('') %}
        <div class="form-text" id="{{ _help_id }}">{{ help }}</div>
    {% endif %}
</fieldset>
